a otra función, por su nombre. Eso es tratar una "},{"type":"definition","term":"funcion-como-valor","text":"función como valor"},{"type":"text","text":". Una función que recibe o devuelve funciones es de "},{"type":"definition","term":"orden-superior","text":"orden superior"},{"type":"text","text":". El tipo de un parámetro que es una función dice qué recibe y qué devuelve: "},{"type":"code","tokens":[["Function","keywordProcedural"],["(","punctuation"],["Integer","type"],[")","punctuation"],[" "],["As","punctuation"],[" "],["Integer","type"]]},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"program","id":"aplicar-dos-veces","title":"Aplicar dos veces","source":"Function siguiente <- MasUno(x As Integer)\n  Define siguiente As Integer;\n  siguiente <- x + 1;\nEndFunction\n\nFunction resultado2 <- AplicarDosVeces(f As Function(Integer) As Integer, x As Integer)\n  Define resultado2 As Integer;\n  resultado2 <- f(f(x));\nEndFunction\n\nAlgorithm Dos\n  Write AplicarDosVeces(MasUno, 5);\nEndAlgorithm\n","lines":[[["Function","keywordProcedural"],[" "],["siguiente","identifier"],[" "],["<-","operator"],[" "],["MasUno","identifier"],["(","punctuation"],["x","identifier"],[" "],["As","punctuation"],[" "],["Integer","type"],[")","punctuation"]],[["  "],["Define","keywordStructured"],[" "],["siguiente","identifier"],[" "],["As","punctuation"],[" "],["Integer","type"],[";","punctuation"]],[["  "],["siguiente","identifier"],[" "],["<-","operator"],[" "],["x","identifier"],[" "],["+","operator"],[" "],["1","literalNumber"],[";","punctuation"]],[["EndFunction","keywordProcedural"]],[],[["Function","keywordProcedural"],[" "],["resultado2","identifier"],[" "],["<-","operator"],[" "],["AplicarDosVeces","identifier"],["(","punctuation"],["f","identifier"],[" "],["As","punctuation"],[" "],["Function","keywordProcedural"],["(","punctuation"],["Integer","type"],[")","punctuation"],[" "],["As","punctuation"],[" "],["Integer","type"],[",","punctuation"],[" "],["x","identifier"],[" "],["As","punc